        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(docker): execute Compose and package artifact proofs",
        "body": "Closes #101039\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where the Docker Compose and package-artifact QA scenarios could pass from helper-level assertions without launching the documented Compose services or installing and executing the real package tarball in a target container.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe scenarios now run through the existing Docker scheduler, image catalog, package builder, and shared script-evidence writer. `compose-setup` starts the documented Gateway and CLI topology from the package-backed functional image. `docker-package-install` installs the canonical tarball in the scheduler-selected bare image. Both record exact package, image, and container identities.\n\nThe package scripts use the concise names `test:docker:compose-setup` and `test:docker:package-install`. The evidence producer and identity writer are TypeScript; the two orchestration entrypoints remain shell because they source the shared timeout/resource/package/image helpers in `scripts/lib/docker-e2e-image.sh` rather than duplicating that contract.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no product runtime change. Routine `smoke-ci` QA remains container-free for these scenarios, while the `release` profile and explicit targeted runs execute the real package and Compose proofs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox: provider `blacksmith-testbox`, id `tbx_01kwwe59na8t8831nkap79zgr0`.\n- Focused validation: formatting and shell syntax passed; 246 focused assertions passed; `pnpm tsgo` passed.\n- Package install proof: `openclaw@2026.6.11`, package sha256 `7eb6cda947fcf86466e639c1e766613a91c4f06f4c5a3a80ea71748d582bee5f`, bare image `sha256:2e76c6d3b08651cfed33c26d144ad794a027c2dfe5a4600fd67397d87fa287db`, target container `3ca6527cdd63ee28332f6f3f9155ce729ae2705a8a127a585f314c6d3753c476`; installed CLI version and help commands passed.\n- Compose proof: same package tarball, functional image `sha256:2fa0d2f4b01ff5112234a9c7a0f42fed719162f96d8e4554bb4f45d228a5b90c`, Gateway container `a178aedda6b0f5f8ddfe5de2b08c3fbecaff8a174270de4ca79849645b1247c1`, CLI container `d5b6c9cab8d702c1a241609397f59dc5ed8c8b5a186e47eaf35fb2fc93267425`; Gateway and CLI health commands passed.\n- Fresh local-change autoreview: clean, with no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted change; implementation and evidence were reviewed and validated as described above.\n",
